# Training text — never committed.
#
# corpus.jsonl holds full problem statements pulled from upstream datasets while
# the model is being fitted. Ledger trains on them and publishes only the
# resulting n-gram weights; redistributing the statements themselves is exactly
# what we don't do. The catalog (metadata + labels, no prose) and the model
# artifact ARE committed.
